==Inventory setups==
In all setups, [[chaos rune]]s must be brought in order to cast [[Crumble Undead]], along with [[dust rune]]s (or [[Air rune|air]] and [[earth rune]]s). A [[rune pouch]] (or its [[Divine rune pouch|divine variant]]) can be used to significantly reduce the number of inventory slots needed. As air and earth runes will already be brought, [[law rune]]s can be brought to cast [[Teleport to House]] as a cheap teleport option.

[[Fire rune|Fire]] and [[nature rune]]s can also be brought to cast [[High Level Alchemy]] on Vorkath's valuable drops, but will take up additional inventory space. With a divine rune pouch, nature runes can be brought without taking up an extra inventory space, and a low quantity of fire runes (20-30) can be brought outside of it, with leftovers being dropped at the site to free up the space for more loot.

Much of the value of Vorkath's drops is in its guaranteed drop of [[superior dragon bones]]. To save space in inventory without a significant loss in profit, if not all bones can be picked up at once, a [[pestle and mortar]] and [[reagent pouch]] can be brought to convert the bones to [[crushed superior dragon bones]], which can be stored in the pouch. Be aware that crushed bones will not sell as quickly as the original version.

A [[Huntsman's kit]] with multiple [[Imp-in-a-box]] stored inside can also be used to effectively increase the number of drops that can be picked up.

